*_precold_*/
derivatives_*/
results_*/

# Archive and literature
archive/
literature/
MANUSCRIPT_CORRECTIONS.md

# Documents, and everything used to fill or check them.
#
# The repository is the code that produces derivatives and results, and it stops
# there. How a number gets from `results/` into a manuscript -- the submission
# files, the plans, the reportable map, and the tooling under `docs/tools/` that
# writes and verifies them -- is authoring, not pipeline, and stays local.
#
# `docs/tools/*.py` IS code, and ignoring code looks like an oversight. It is not:
# those scripts open .docx files and edit prose. Do not add an un-ignore rule for
# them. Nothing tracked here opens a document -- the steps name Tables and Figures
# in their docstrings to say what their output feeds, and write only to `results/`.
docs/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Document tooling and spent scaffolding. This repository generates results; anything
# that reads or writes a .docx lives with the documents, under docs/tools/, and the
# one-shot revision scripts were archived on 11 Aug 2026 to codes/python/archive/.
# Both are already covered by the archive/ and docs/ rules above; named here so it is
# obvious the omission is deliberate rather than an oversight.
codes/python/archive/
codes/python/revision/
